# Docker build context hygiene for the bonsai2 build pipeline (MAP 1.2).
# The Dockerfile's only COPY is third_party/llama.cpp/ -> /src; everything
# else in the repo root is excluded to keep the context small.
#
# NOTE: we exclude the 4 root docs by name (NOT a blanket `*.md`) so the
# fork's own .md files under third_party/llama.cpp/ (README, AGENTS, ...)
# stay in context. The build does not read them today (no CMake `read()`
# of .md at the pin), but if the fork ever adds a required .md at configure
# time, a blanket `*.md` here would ENOENT it — the named entries keep that
# failure visible rather than silent.
.git
.gitmodules
# gitlink form: a submodule's .git is a regular *file* in the working
# tree; this entry excludes it. The pattern is path-based (not
# type-based), so it also excludes a `third_party/llama.cpp/.git`
# *directory* if the submodule is ever replaced by a plain nested
# clone — the context stays small and the "COPY has no git metadata"
# assumption in the Dockerfile header holds in either form.
third_party/llama.cpp/.git
test-logs/
docs/
bench-results/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
# scr.txt: tracked scratch file (also in .gitignore) — keep excluded.
scr.txt
# Root project docs (not fork source):
AGENTS.md
ARTIFACTS.md
MAP.md
SPEC.md
